WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.790
Two healthy people.

2
00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:04.200
Each has perfectly good blood.

3
00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:09.720
Give one person's blood to the other, and
the reaction can be severe, even fatal.

4
00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:13.230
Yet many pairs can give
and receive blood safely.

5
00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:16.240
Hospitals match blood
before a transfusion.

6
00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:20.460
So what makes the difference
between safe blood and deadly blood?

7
00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:24.520
In this mission, you'll find out
what really makes your blood group A,

8
00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:27.060
B, AB or O.

9
00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:32.080
Then you'll read a typing test: drops
of blood mixed with two test serums,

10
00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:34.280
anti-A and anti-B.

11
00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:39.320
Your mission: find out why blood from one
healthy person can be deadly to another

12
00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:40.360
healthy person.
